d it rewarding to see the dialogue she wrote acted out, noting it was the third time this happened. Seeing characters and dialogue from her writing performed was an amazing experience.\n  - dreams: Joanna's book covered sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams; she finished writing and editing it last week. Joanna encourages reaching for dreams.\n  - fruit: Joanna commented that some characters look like they really enjoy fruit.\n  - journey: Joanna values the journey, appreciating happy moments to stay focused on dreams, and looks forward to showing it to Nate.\n  - writing inspiration: Joanna uses taking breaks and self-care for writing inspiration to maintain inspiration and mental health, seeking balance.\n  - dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness: Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - creatures: Joanna noted that the creatures bring much calm and joy, and asked if taking care of them is tough.\n  - personal experiences and feelings: Joanna shared that meaningful stories arise from vulnerability, exploring personal experiences and feelings, and remaining true to oneself, as acknowledged by Nate.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - talent: Nate encouraged Joanna, affirming her incredible talent and promising her hard work will pay off. Joanna is using a road trip for research for her next movie.\n  - acting: Joanna enjoys acting, especially dramas and emotionally-driven films, and might try it if given the opportunity while currently focusing on her writers group.\n  - gorgeous sunset: Joanna took a picture of a gorgeous sunset while hiking near Fort Wayne last summer; Nate asked what inspired the photo.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience 