, for a slow introduction to Toby and Buddy.\n  - German Shepherd: Andrew's pup, Toby, is a German Shepherd and loves cute sweaters; he is described as active.\n  - adventures: Audrey's dogs are set for their next outdoor adventure, following a recent grooming session. Andrew previously found dogs tough due to housing.\n  - dog: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon for grooming. Andrew adopted another dog recently, managing with two dogs currently, and asked Audrey for multi-dog owner tips.\n  - Andrew's pup: Andrew's pup is a German Shepherd known for loyalty and smarts. Andrew is going camping with his girlfriend, Toby, and the pup.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - Andrew's GF: Andrew's GF, Toby, played board games with Andrew last Tuesday. Andrew's GF is mentioned in relation to a sweet sweater and possibly visiting a dog park.\n  - new pups: Andrew is looking to adopt a doggo after browsing websites, visiting shelters, and asking friends. Audrey mentioned that meeting new pups brings happiness.\n  - breed: Andrew asked Audrey about her dogs' breed and what they enjoy doing most, following a discussion about dog training and finding dog-friendly spots.\n  - doggo: Audrey groomed her dogs, who looked cute with shiny coats after being good at the salon. Andrew adopted another dog and shared a photo.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - Andrew's girlfriend: Andrew's girlfriend creates a safe and fun space for Scout, and she is encouraged to slowly introduce Scout to Toby and Buddy.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - Andrew (assistant): Andrew asked Audrey about the tips she received from her dogs' appointment with an animal behaviorist. Andrew suggested visiting a lake near a trail to see the autumn colors.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - doggy daycare: Andrew mentioned a doggy daycare near him that has a big indoor space for dogs to play.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - rug: Panda, one of Audrey's four dogs, loves to relax on his rug.\n  - sunny days: Audrey's dogs hate snow and prefer nice, sunny days spent in the grass.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - water: Audrey's dogs enjoyed playing in the ocean water at the beach over the weekend.\n  - couch: Pepper, one of Audrey's four dogs, loves lounging on the couch.\n  - Pepper: Pepper is one of Audrey's four dogs, described as a Lab mix. Audrey has four dogs: Pepper, Panda, Precious, and Pixie.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - pooches: Pooches moved to a new place with a bigger backyard for running and exploring. Audrey calmed her pooch, Precious, by petting, hugging, and speaking calmly; patience and practice help establish bonds with pooches.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2054,"context_chars":7765,"retrieval_duration":0.20976734161376953,"response_duration":2.367546558380127,"total_duration":2.5773138999938965,"grad