e some art; Melanie finds art calming and expressive, and Caroline previously made pottery and attended a poetry reading.\n  - LGBTQ+ counseling workshop: Caroline attended an LGBTQ+ counseling workshop last Friday about therapeutic methods for working with and supporting the mental health of trans people.\n  - school event: Caroline attended a school event last week where she discussed her transgender journey and encouraged student involvement in the LGBTQ community, reflecting on her transition started three years ago.\n  - pride parade: Caroline attended a pride parade last Friday, describing it as awesome with much energy and love, reinforcing the importance of equality.\n  - safe space: Caroline attended an LGBTQ+ counseling workshop last Friday where pros were passionate about making a safe space for trans people.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - Caroline's Web: Melanie read \"Charlotte's Web\" as a child and appreciated how it showed the impact of friendship and compassion.\n  - \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles: Caroline finds \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles significant as it represents courage and fighting for what is right, reminding her of her progress.\n  - identities: Identities were celebrated and shared through poetry at a transgender poetry reading, creating a safe and empowering space for self-expression.\n  - artist: Caroline, an artist, attended a pride parade last Friday and was asked by Melanie about how she stays inclusive in her work.\n  - inspiring stories: Caroline attended an LGBTQ support group yesterday and Melanie inquired about any inspiring stories heard there.\n  - kids in need: Melanie's kids made things with clay. Caroline attended a council meeting about adoption, which made her more determined to adopt children in need.\n  - transgender conference: Caroline attended a