g yoga, following a retreat in Phuket.\n  - yoga pose: Jolene's partner performed a yoga pose after a trip to Rio de Janeiro. Jolene asked if the pose helps the partner relax.\n  - yoga on the beach: Jolene expressed interest in trying yoga on the beach and asked if it is a common activity.\n  - healthy habit: Jolene is thankful for her partner encouraging her goals and is excited to attend a meditation course at a lake retreat. She notes that an easy habit makes a big health difference.\n  - yoga event: Deborah organized a yoga event last month, which she enjoyed and found cool. Jolene later asked for details on how it was put together.\n  - break from life: Jolene uses 'break from life' as a way to de-stress and take a break from life.\n  - yoga retreat: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat described as peaceful with amazing sunrise views, making attendees feel alive and grateful. Deborah inquires about a future experience.\n  - poses: Deborah mentioned a favorite yoga routine involves a gentle flow focused on breathing and grounding, and will send Jolene a tutorial video with the poses.\n  - meditation course: Jolene signed up for a meditation course at a retreat near a lake, excited to share it with her partner and learn new techniques.\n  - something that helps you cope: Jolene mentioned that finding 'something that helps you cope' after losing someone is great.\n  - meditation: Jolene uses meditation for self-care, planning a camping trip. She recently tried a new style of meditation with flowers in Thailand.\n  - bullet journal: Jolene uses a bullet journal to track tasks and stay organized, finding satisfaction in crossing off items on her list.\n  - mindfulness: Jolene realized the importance of mindfulness, self-care, and balance alongside engineering studies after a meditation retreat in Phuket. Deborah encourages this practice.\n  - beauties: Jolene encourages Deborah to keep finding 'beauties', following a conversation about music festivals and a yog