ing trip. She recently tried a new style of meditation with flowers in Thailand.\n  - mount Talkeetna: Jolene spent yesterday morning doing yoga on top of mount Talkeetna.\n  - meditation course: Jolene signed up for a meditation course at a retreat near a lake, excited to share it with her partner and learn new techniques.\n  - progress: Deborah noted positive progress; Jolene feels calmer, clearer, alert, and motivated after meditating, breathing, or doing yoga, following a retreat in Phuket.\n  - meditate: Jolene finds calm when she meditates, often using essential oils and soft music. Deborah previously meditated as part of her routine.\n  - Jolene's partner: Jolene's partner has values that encourage pursuing creative endeavors. They recently returned from a trip to Rio de Janeiro with Jolene, where they tried yoga classes.\n  - meditation routine: Jolene signed up for a meditation course at a retreat near a lake; Deborah uses meditation as a routine part of life.\n  - yoga: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat; doing yoga with a beautiful sunrise backdrop made her feel connected to nature, peaceful, and thankful.\n  - mindfulness: Jolene realized the importance of mindfulness, self-care, and balance alongside engineering studies after a meditation retreat in Phuket. Deborah encourages this practice.\n  - yoga on the beach: Jolene expressed interest in trying yoga on the beach and asked if it is a common activity.\n  - yoga classes: Jolene and her partner went to Rio de Janeiro, where they checked out and appreciated learning about different kinds of yoga and their backgrounds in cool yoga classes.\n  - Susie: Jolene mentioned that Susie is a great companion. Jolene has had Susie for two years.\n  - work stress: Work stress is something that Jolene has been escaping for 3 years by playing a game.\n  - calming the mind: Jolene asked for advice on calming the mind and breathing during yoga; Deborah confirmed a studio is calming.\n  - yoga event: Deborah organi